            "review_title": "Review at Chả cá Kẻ Chợ",
            "review_text": "Ryan\n3 contributions\n0\nA meal in Hanoi that was more memorable than pho\nAug 2026 • Family\nA meal in Hanoi that was more memorable than pho\n\nIt would be a bit of a shame to come to Hanoi and only eat pho and bun cha before leaving.\nThis city has a special fish dish, **Chả Cá**, which is cooked sizzling on a pan.\n\nAmong them, Chả Cá Kẻ Chợ is a place that is not yet widely known to tourists.\n\nThe signature 'Kẻ Chợ' here is a little special.\nSake reduces the fishy smell, and it is seasoned twice with about 30 spices to deepen the flavor. Large pieces of fish are generously filled with dill and scallions, and the staff cooks it right at the table, and the aroma rising from the pan already stimulates the appetite.\n\nWith rice vermicelli (Bún), peanuts, and herbs, and a touch of Vietnamese fermented shrimp paste **mắm tôm**, you get a burst of nutty, fragrant, and savory flavors in every bite. If you're worried about the smell of mắm tôm, try adding some lemon juice. It becomes much milder and a flavor you keep thinking about.\n\nIt's not crowded like a famous restaurant in a tourist spot, and the interior is bright and clean.\nIf you want to try real local food that others don't know about in Hanoi, this is a place worth going to intentionally.\n\n📍 Ca Ca Kẻ Chợ\n175 Nguyen Tuan, Thanh Xuan, Hanoi\n⏰ 10:00–14:00 / 17:00–22:00\n\nAfter taking the first bite, you will probably think this.\nWhy did I only find out this on the last day of my Hanoi trip?\n\n#HanoiFood #HanoiTravel #Chaca #VietnameseFood #HanoiLocalFood #ChacaKeCho\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten August 30, 2026",
