            "review_text": "Navigate61220508627\nHanoi, Vietnam3 contributions\n0\nA chakra shop I found in the neighborhood that I want to go to again\nAug 2026 • Friends\nI live near Tain Suan Ward and saw it on a blog for Japanese people living in Hanoi, so I was curious and went.\n\nThe chakara has a good aroma of dill and green onion, and it doesn't get boring even if eaten with bun and peanuts. I tried Mamutom little by little, and it was helpful that I could switch to Nuckmam if it wasn't to my liking.\n\nI also ordered \"cá lăng xông đá lửa.\" It was interesting that it was served to the table in a style where the scent was added with a heated stone. It was memorable with a different flavor than Charka.\n\nThe restaurant is clean inside, and it's a place I want to go to again when I want to eat Vietnamese food slowly nearby.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten August 30, 2026",
